# E24 -- Does entry quantity set how MUCH surface life a fort sees, or only which species are eligible? E36 showed that on the cavern layer frequency divides a fixed spawn budget rather than setting volume — a 25-fold cut moved one pair to zero while the total held. The same discriminator is applied here to the surface layer's own lever: the roster is run at in_season_qty 200 against 20, a tenfold difference in every managed land entry, same species, same seasons. If total surface arrivals scale with it, the abundance slider sets volume; if they hold, it only gates. A season, two replicates each.
run 20260918-170239 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
commits: DwarfCron 835fddb seasonal-wildlife 41bbd19 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- quantity sets volume: total surface arrivals rise clearly with in_season_qty — roughly with the tenfold difference, or at least unmistakably
- quantity only gates (a shared budget, as the caverns have): total surface arrivals are about the same in both arms; the pool numbers differ tenfold and the map does not
- quantity matters only near zero: no difference between 20 and 200, but both far above what a zeroed roster gives — the lever is on/off with a wide flat middle

